      "A microcontroller interacts with the external environment using input/output (I/O) ports. Inputs allow the microcontroller to sense changes in the environment, while outputs enable it to control devices. A push button is one of the simplest digital input devices, and an LED is a simple digital output device. This experiment combines both to demonstrate basic I/O handling using the PIC18F4520 microcontroller.",
