      "The PIC18F4520 has several TRIS (Tri-State) registers to configure pins as input (1) or output (0). For example, if a pin is configured as input, the microcontroller only reads its state but does not drive it. Similarly, LAT (Latch) and PORT registers are used to write and read data to/from ports.",
