      "Timer2 + CCP1 PWM mode → continuous square wave with programmable frequency and duty.",
      "Timer1 + CCP1 Compare (toggle) or Timer ISR → exact user-defined frequencies, good for learning timer math.",
      "Using PWM mode with 50% duty is simplest for a clean, continuous square wave on the CCP1 pin (RC2). Frequency is set by Timer2’s prescaler and PR2. Alternatively, a Timer1 interrupt can toggle any GPIO at precise half-period intervals (good for understanding timing calculations).",
      "// CCP1 (RC2) will output the PWM square wave",
      "// RC2 as output",
      "// Timer2 setup: Prescale = 16, PR2 = 311 -> ~1 kHz",
      "// 50% duty: CCPR1L:DC1B = 624 -> 156:0",
      "CCPR1L = 156; // upper 8 duty bits",
      "// PWM mode on CCP1",
